---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED, OPERATOR } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout title="Terms of use">
	<main class="container page narrow prose">
		<div>
			<h1>Terms of use</h1>
			<p class="muted">Last updated {LEGAL_UPDATED}</p>
		</div>

		<section>
			<p>EduTrack is a free study log run by {OPERATOR}. By creating an account you accept these terms.</p>

			<h2>Your account</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>You sign in with your own Google account and are responsible for what is done with your account.</li>
				<li>Pick a username that does not impersonate someone else and is not offensive.</li>
				<li>You can delete your account at any time on the <a href="/app/account">Account</a> page.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Courses you add</h2>
			<p>
				Courses you create are shared with all students at your university. Enter the real course code and name. Administrators may rename,
				merge or remove courses to keep the list correct.
			</p>

			<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
			<p>
				Do not misuse the service, for example by trying to access other people's data, overloading the site or entering offensive content.
				We may suspend or delete accounts that break these terms.
			</p>

			<h2>No guarantees</h2>
			<p>
				EduTrack is provided as it is, free of charge. We do our best to keep it running and your data safe, but we cannot guarantee that
				the service is always available or free of errors, and we are not liable for lost data or for decisions based on the statistics.
				The service may change or shut down. If it shuts down we will tell users in advance where possible.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version. Significant changes will be announced on the site.</p>

			<h2>Contact and law</h2>
			<p>
				Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Swedish law applies. Read how we handle personal data in the
				<a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
